        "step_title": "SynoCli WiFi Tools",
        "items": [
            {
                "desc": "The tools to connect the NAS to a WiFi network, with the adapters of <b>synokernel-wifi</b>: load the driver of the adapter with <b>synocli-kernelmodule</b>, then connect with <b>wifi-connect</b> and the profile of the network:<br><br><code>synocli-kernelmodule list</code><br><code>sudo -i synocli-kernelmodule --profile rtl88x2bu start</code><br><code>sudo -i wifi-connect MyNetwork</code><br><br><code>sudo -i wifi-connect --new</code> writes the profile of another network, <code>--list</code>, <code>--status</code> and <code>--stop</code> do what they say. See the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://docs.synocommunity.com/packages/synocli-wifi-tools/\">package documentation</a>."
            }
        ]
    }
]
